.TH BEAM 1 beam\-VERSION
.SH NAME
beam \- ephemeral file and video sharing utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beam
.RB [ \-1cfFpqrvw ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR ttl ]
.RB [ \-k
.IR token ]
.RB [ \-H
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-b
.IR ip ]
.RB [ \-P
.IR port ]
.RI [ file \ |\  \- ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B beam
serves a local file over HTTP using a temporary, random URL.
.P
When sharing video, browsers open their native media player.
.B beam
handles HTTP 206 Partial Content range requests so browsers can seek through
MP4 and WebM files without downloading the entire file first.
.P
The URL path contains a random 32-character hex token from /dev/urandom
(for example,
.IR https://5369e9d69bbb03.lhr.life/4bdaa908ed74c21a9f03b8e1d5a7c6e2 ).
.P
The
.B \-p
option starts a Cloudflare quick tunnel
.RB ( cloudflared )
so remote players hit HTTPS at the edge instead of an SSH forward.
.B beam
renders an ANSI QR code in the terminal using Unicode half-blocks and exits
when the lifetime timer expires (default: 5 hours).
.P
If no file argument is given,
.B beam
automatically reopens the last beamed file and preserves its token so the
previous link stays live. If piped, it reads standard input and prioritizes
dubbed video files over subtitles and logs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " ttl"
Set link lifetime. Suffixes
.BR s " (seconds),"
.BR m " (minutes),"
.BR h " (hours),"
or
.BR d " (days)"
are supported. Default is
.BR 5h .
.TP
.B \-p
Open an ephemeral public HTTPS tunnel via cloudflared. Requires
.B cloudflared
on PATH. Override the binary with
.BR BEAM_TUNNEL_BIN .
.TP
.B \-r
Reopen and resume the last beamed file and token.
.TP
.BI \-k " token"
Specify an explicit 12-character token hash.
.TP
.BI \-H " host"
Specify the host, IP address, or domain name to use in the share link (for example,
.BR 192.168.1.50
or
.BR mynode.ts.net ).
.TP
.B \-c
Copy the share URL to the system clipboard using
.BR clipbridge ,
.BR wl-copy ,
.BR xclip ,
.BR pbcopy ,
or
.BR clip.exe .
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode. Suppress the terminal QR code.
.TP
.B \-1
One-shot mode. Exit after the first complete file download or view.
.TP
.B \-f
Force an MP4 faststart remux with ffmpeg so the index sits at the start of the file.
.TP
.B \-F
Skip MP4 faststart remuxing.
.TP
.B \-w
Serve an HTML player wrapper instead of the raw media stream.
.TP
.BI \-b " ip"
Specify the IP address to bind to. Default is
.BR 0.0.0.0 .
.TP
.BI \-P " port"
Specify the port to listen on. Default is
.BR 8080 ,
or the next available port.
.TP
.B \-v
Print version information and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
While
.B beam
is running in a terminal, single keystrokes can trigger actions:
.TP
.B p
Open or reopen the public HTTPS tunnel.
.TP
.B c
Copy the share link to the system clipboard.
.TP
.B q
Quit and close the link.
.SH EXAMPLES
Share a video locally with default 5-hour lifetime:
.IP
.EX
beam dubbed_video.mp4
.EE
.P
Pipe from autodub to share a newly dubbed video publicly:
.IP
.EX
autodub "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=icsP8f8TRdQ" | beam -p -c
.EE
.P
Reopen the last beamed video over the public tunnel with the same link:
.IP
.EX
beam -p -c
.EE
.P
Share a file using a Tailscale hostname:
.IP
.EX
beam -H mynode.ts.net -c dubbed_video.mp4
.EE
.P
Share an archive valid for 30 minutes in one-shot mode:
.IP
.EX
beam -t 30m -1 archive.zip
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR autodub (1)
.SH AUTHORS
